<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Push. `development` here: Xcode rewrites it to `production` when it
		exports a build for TestFlight or the App Store, and the running app
		reads which one it got from its provisioning profile
		(LiaisonNativePlugin.apsEnvironment) so the server sends each token to
		the matching APNs host.

		App Group `group.sh.liaison.mobile`: shared with the Notification
		Service Extension (NotificationService/), which leaves its state there
		for the app to read.

		Keychain group `$(AppIdentifierPrefix)sh.liaison.mobile`: the app's
		own, listed first so the refresh token defaults to it.
		Keychain group `$(AppIdentifierPrefix)sh.liaison.mobile.shared`: the
		receipt credentials, written by the app, read by the extension.

		Nothing else. No associated domains: universal links need an
		association file served from each operator's own host, and a domain
		named here is baked into a binary every fork ships. Links into the
		app use the `liaison` scheme. Every entitlement in this file is
		something the provisioning profile has to grant: one that is not is a
		signing failure, not a missing feature.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.sh.liaison.mobile</string>
	</array>
	<!-- The app's own keychain group FIRST: an item written without naming a
	     group (the refresh token, auth/secret-store.ts) lands in the first
	     group listed, and the extension must never read the session.
	     Then the group shared with the Notification Service Extension: the app
	     stores each server's receipt-only credential there, naming it, and the
	     extension reads it to post `received` (ReceiptStore.swift, spec-push A7). -->
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)sh.liaison.mobile</string>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)sh.liaison.mobile.shared</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
